{"id":"000VXC","title":"Split Peas Lies","author":"raaaaa","solvedCount":2,"difficulty":4,"rating":"N/A","firstSeen":"2026-11-07T02:55:37+00:00","posted":"Heute, 02:00 Uhr","rules":"This puzzle was inspired by\nmarty_sears's\nLiar Cell series.\nMany thanks also to\nSamuPiano\nfor creating the Split Peas Lines constraint.\n\nClick the image to play this puzzle.\n\nRules:\n\nNormal sudoku rules apply.\n\nLIAR CELLS:\n\nEvery row, column and 3x3 box contains one liar cell, whose real value is different from its digit. Every other cell's value is its digit.\n\n• Every liar cell contains a different digit from 1-9.\n\n• Every liar cell has a different value from 1-9.\n\nSPLIT PEAS LINES:\n\nThe values of cells strictly between the two circles on a green line sum to a two-digit number formed by the values in those circles, in either order. Values may repeat on a line. Different lines may share endpoint circles.\n\nBLACK DOTS:\n\nCells separated by a black dot have values in a 1:2 ratio.\n\nWHITE DOTS:\n\nCells separated by a white dot have consecutive values.\n\nX / V:\n\nThe values of two cells separated by an X sum to 10; those separated by a V sum to 5. Not all dots or X/V clues are given.\n\nNOTES:\n\nIn each arrow, record its row's liar digit. In the circle to its right, record that liar cell's real value. Filling in these notes is optional.","solutionCode":"The VALUES in row 2, from left to right (9 digits).","tags":["Sudoku"],"links":[{"url":"https://sudokupad.app/8ms3im2fhi","kind":"sudokupad"}],"data":"","error":null,"settings":{},"link":"https://sudokupad.app/8ms3im2fhi","linkKind":"sudokupad","summary":{"format":"scl","decoded":true,"rows":9,"cols":11,"cages":0,"hasSolution":true,"features":["lines","overlays","underlays"]},"attempts":0,"fetched":"2026-11-07T02:55:37+00:00"}